1. Surgery Gap Theorem: equation dependency chain

The primitive starting equations are:

$$ \boxed{u=\Pi_\alpha X_\alpha} \tag{S1} $$

and the internal correction equation

$$ \boxed{d_\alpha+\mathcal A_\alpha(W)=0.} \tag{S2} $$

Equation S2 is equivalent to

$$ \boxed{-d_\alpha\in\operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_\alpha.} \tag{S3} $$

The gap begins with the negation:

$$ \boxed{-d_\alpha\notin\operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_{\alpha,\mathrm{all}}.} \tag{S4} $$

That equation is the core obstruction. By contradiction, S4 implies

$$ \boxed{\nexists W\;:\;d_\alpha+\mathcal A_\alpha(W)=0.} \tag{S5} $$

Now add lossless representation transformation

$$ \boxed{ \mathcal A_\beta T_{\alpha\beta} = T_{\alpha\beta}\mathcal A_\alpha. } \tag{S6} $$

From S6:

$$ -d_\alpha\in\operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_\alpha \iff -T_{\alpha\beta}d_\alpha \in \operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_\beta. \tag{S7} $$

Therefore if S4 survives all such \(T\),

$$ \boxed{ -d_{T(\alpha)} \notin \operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_{T(\alpha)} \quad \forall T\in RC. } \tag{S8} $$

Next comes normalization exclusion:

$$ \boxed{ -d_{N(\alpha)} \notin \operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_{N(\alpha)} \quad \forall N\in\mathcal N. } \tag{S9} $$

Then physical-lift exclusion:

$$ \boxed{ \nexists W_\alpha \text{ admissible such that } \Pi_\alpha W_\alpha=c_{\rm phys}. } \tag{S10} $$

S4 + S8 + S9 + S10 yield:

$$ \boxed{ D_S \notin \operatorname{Closure}_{RC,\mathcal A,\mathcal N,\Pi} (\mathcal X_\alpha). } \tag{S11} $$

Now establish an alternate sector:

$$ \boxed{ -d_\beta\in\operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_\beta. } \tag{S12} $$

Hence

$$ \boxed{ \exists W_\beta: d_\beta+\mathcal A_\beta(W_\beta)=0. } \tag{S13} $$

Finally impose shadow preservation:

$$ \boxed{ \Pi_\beta S_{\alpha\to\beta}X_\alpha = \Pi_\alpha X_\alpha. } \tag{S14} $$

Define

$$ \Omega_R^-(d) = \{\mathcal R:-d_\mathcal R\notin\operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_\mathcal R\}, $$ $$ \Omega_R^+(d) = \{\mathcal R:-d_\mathcal R\in\operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_\mathcal R\}. \tag{S15} $$

Then S11 + S12 + S14 give:

$$ \boxed{ \Omega_R^-(d) \xrightarrow{S_{\alpha\to\beta}} \Omega_R^+(d), \qquad \Pi_\beta S_{\alpha\to\beta}X = \Pi_\alpha X. } \tag{S16} $$

And therefore:

$$ \boxed{\text{genuine Surgery gap}.} \tag{S17} $$

So the compressed dependency DAG is

$$ \boxed{ \begin{array}{c} S2\leftrightarrow S3\\ \downarrow\\ S4\Rightarrow S5\\ \downarrow\\ S6\Rightarrow S7\Rightarrow S8\\ \downarrow\\ S9,\;S10\\ \downarrow\\ S11\\ +\;S12\Rightarrow S13\\ +\;S14\\ \downarrow\\ S16\\ \downarrow\\ S17 \end{array}} $$

That is essentially the equation skeleton of the uploaded Surgery Gap theorem.

2. NS Surgery Gap: equation dependencies

The NS specialization adds only a few equations to the abstract chain.

Sector decomposition:

$$ \boxed{ \mathcal X = \bigsqcup_{\kappa\in K}\mathcal X_\kappa. } \tag{NS1} $$

Fixed-sector regular evolution preserves sector:

$$ \boxed{ X(t)\in\mathcal X_\kappa^{\rm reg} \Longrightarrow \kappa(t)=\kappa. } \tag{NS2} $$

But the required continuation demands

$$ \boxed{\kappa'\neq\kappa.} \tag{NS3} $$

Suppose an internal Wing did it:

$$ d_\kappa+\mathcal A_\kappa(W_\kappa)=0. \tag{NS4} $$

Then NS2 would force

$$ \kappa'=\kappa, $$

contradicting NS3.

Therefore

$$ \boxed{ -d_\kappa\notin\operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_\kappa. } \tag{NS5} $$

The Surgery map is

$$ \boxed{ S_{\kappa\to\kappa'}: \mathcal X_\kappa\to\mathcal X_{\kappa'}. } \tag{NS6} $$

with

$$ \boxed{ \Pi_{\kappa'} S_{\kappa\to\kappa'}X = \Pi_\kappa X. } \tag{NS7} $$

Thus:

$$ \boxed{ \mathcal X_\kappa^{\rm reg} \to \partial\mathcal X_\kappa^{\rm reg} \xrightarrow{S_{\kappa\to\kappa'}} \mathcal X_{\kappa'}^{\rm reg}. } \tag{NS8} $$

So:

$$ \boxed{ NS1+NS2+NS3 \Rightarrow NS5 \Rightarrow NS6+NS7 \Rightarrow NS8. } $$

That is the actual minimal NS Surgery equation chain.

3. Unknown Discovery Gap: equation dependencies

Now leave physical geometry and move into the discovery theorem.

The primitive equation is:

$$ \boxed{ D_S \notin \operatorname{Closure}_{RC,\mathcal A}(K^-). } \tag{G1} $$

Let \(Z_S\) select the correct missing direction.

Then G1 implies residual uncertainty:

$$ \boxed{ H(Z_S\mid K^-)>0. } \tag{G2} $$

Define opacity:

$$ \boxed{ O_S=H(Z_S\mid K^-). } \tag{G3} $$

For a uniform residual candidate space,

$$ \boxed{ N=2^{O_S}. } \tag{G4} $$

Closed reasoning evolves by

$$ \boxed{ K_{n+1}=F_n(K_n,R_n), } \tag{G5} $$

with

$$ R_n\perp Z_S. $$

Therefore data processing yields

$$ \boxed{ I(Z_S;K_n) \le I(Z_S;K^-). } \tag{G6} $$

So closed inference cannot reduce G2 by manufacturing new target-correlated information.

If there are \(N\) residual candidates and \(k\) successful ones, and \(B\) candidates can be tested,

$$ \boxed{ P_{\rm hit} = 1- \frac{\binom{N-k}{B}}{\binom NB}. } \tag{G7} $$

Union bound:

$$ \boxed{ P_{\rm hit} \le \frac{Bk}{N}. } \tag{G8} $$

Substitute G4:

$$ \boxed{ P_{\rm hit} \le Bk\,2^{-O_S}. } \tag{G9} $$

So:

$$ \boxed{ G1\Rightarrow G2\Rightarrow G3\Rightarrow G4 } $$

and independently

$$ \boxed{ G5\Rightarrow G6, } $$

then

$$ \boxed{ G4+G7\Rightarrow G8\Rightarrow G9. } $$

This is the entire discovery-gap/search chain.

4. Multi-agent Gap Theorem: equation dependencies

Let

$$ A=\text{number of agents} $$

and \(m\) useful candidate tests per agent.

Then

$$ \boxed{ M\le Am. } \tag{MA1} $$

From G8:

$$ P_{\rm hit} \le \frac{Mk}{N}. $$

Using MA1:

$$ \boxed{ P_{\rm hit} \le \frac{Amk}{N}. } \tag{MA2} $$

Using \(N=2^{O_S}\):

$$ \boxed{ P_{\rm hit} \le Amk\,2^{-O_S}. } \tag{MA3} $$

For \(A=10{,}000\):

$$ \boxed{ P_{\rm hit} \le 10{,}000\,mk\,2^{-O_S}. } \tag{MA4} $$

For \(A=100\):

$$ \boxed{ P_{\rm hit} \le 100\,mk\,2^{-O_S}. } \tag{MA5} $$

Hence for the same gap and same \(m,k\):

$$ \boxed{ \frac{P_{100}^{\rm bound}} {P_{10k}^{\rm bound}} = \frac{100}{10{,}000} = 0.01. } \tag{MA6} $$

That is the full resource-scaling dependency.

5. Euler Gap Theorem: equation dependencies

The structural Euler theorem is essentially the Surgery chain with Euler labels.

Core obstruction:

$$ \boxed{ -d_{\kappa,E} \notin \operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_{\kappa,E}. } \tag{E1} $$

RC survival:

$$ \boxed{ -d_{T(\kappa),E} \notin \operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_{T(\kappa),E} \quad\forall T. } \tag{E2} $$

Normalization survival:

$$ \boxed{ -d_{N(\kappa),E} \notin \operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_{N(\kappa),E} \quad\forall N. } \tag{E3} $$

No lift:

$$ \boxed{ \nexists W_\kappa: \Pi_\kappa W_\kappa=c_{\rm phys}. } \tag{E4} $$

Together:

$$ \boxed{ D_E \notin \operatorname{Closure}_{RC,\mathcal A,\mathcal N,\Pi}(K_E^-). } \tag{E5} $$

Alternate sector:

$$ \boxed{ -d_{\kappa',E} \in \operatorname{Im}\mathcal A_{\kappa',E}. } \tag{E6} $$

Shadow preservation:

$$ \boxed{ \Pi_{\kappa'} S_{\kappa\to\kappa'}^E X = \Pi_\kappa X. } \tag{E7} $$

Therefore:

$$ \boxed{ \Omega_E^-(d) \xrightarrow{S_E} \Omega_E^+(d). } \tag{E8} $$

That proves the structural Euler Gap.

